## Implementation prompts

Use these prompts in order when building or extending the site.

### Prompt 1: Scaffold

Scaffold the project in this folder: Next.js 15 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + ESLint, using `src/` directory. Set up `next/font` with Cormorant Garamond and Inter. Create a Tailwind theme with the color palette from the project rules. Create a `/data/site.ts` file with placeholders for: broker name, phone, text number, email, office address, brokerage license number, social links, GA4 ID, GTM ID, Meta Pixel ID. Create a `.env.example` listing every environment variable the project will need (Resend API key, CRM API key, lead notification email, Turnstile keys, Meta CAPI token). Initialize git with a sensible `.gitignore`. Confirm it runs with `npm run dev`.

### Prompt 2: Lot data

Create `/data/lots.ts` exporting a typed array of **22 lots**. Lot type fields: `lotNumber`, `slug` (e.g. `"lot-7"`), `address`, `acreage`, `squareFeet`, `price`, `status` (`"available" | "under-contract" | "sold"`), `views` (array, e.g. `"Mt. Timpanogos"`, `"Deer Creek Reservoir"`, `"Meadow"`), `slopeDescription`, `utilities` (water, power, sewer/septic, internet), `buildableAreaNotes`, `highlights` (3–5 bullets), `photos` (array of paths), `videoUrl` (optional), `latitude`, `longitude`, `mapPolygon` (SVG points string for the plat map), `plaPdfPath`.

Fill with realistic placeholder data to edit later; mark every placeholder with a `TODO` comment. Also export helper functions: `getAvailableLots()`, `getLotBySlug()`, `lotsRemainingCount()`, and `priceRange()`.

*(After this prompt, replace the placeholders with real lot data.)*

