### Prompt 11: Tracking and analytics

Implement tracking:

- Google Tag Manager loaded with `next/script` (`afterInteractive`), ID from `/data/site.ts`.
- GA4 via GTM. Push `dataLayer` events: `generate_lead` (with variant and `lotNumber`), `packet_download`, `tour_booked` (listen for Calendly `postMessage` events), `click_to_call`, `click_to_text`, `lot_view` (lot number), `map_lot_click`, `calculator_used`, `exit_popup_shown`, `exit_popup_converted`.
- Meta Pixel with `PageView`, `ViewContent` on lot pages, `Lead` on form submit, `Schedule` on tour booking.
- Meta Conversions API: in `/api/lead`, send a server-side Lead event with hashed email/phone and the same `event_id` as the browser pixel for deduplication.
- Microsoft Clarity script (ID in `site.ts`).
- Simple cookie consent banner (accept/decline) that gates non-essential tracking.
- Document every event in `/docs/tracking.md` so conversions can be set up in GA4, Google Ads, and Meta.

### Prompt 12: Performance and accessibility pass

Do a full performance and accessibility audit and fix everything:

- Run a production build and analyze bundle size; remove or lazy-load anything heavy.
- Verify all images are `next/image` with correct `sizes` attributes and `priority` only on LCP images.
- Defer all third-party scripts (GTM, Clarity, Calendly, chat) until after interaction or idle.
- Check color contrast, focus states, form labels, alt text, and keyboard navigation on the map and modals.
- Add a custom 404 page with links to available lots.
- Report the final Lighthouse mobile scores for home, `/map`, and one lot page, and list anything still below 95 with fixes.

### Prompt 13: Deploy

Walk through deploying to **Vercel** step by step: push this repo to a new private GitHub repo, import it into Vercel, add every environment variable from `.env.example`, connect the custom domain `[YOURDOMAIN.com]` with `www` redirecting to the root domain, and verify the Resend sending domain DNS records. If the old Étienne site has existing URLs, create `next.config` redirects (301) from those old URLs to the matching new pages: `[PASTE OLD URLS]`. Then provide a post-launch checklist: submit the sitemap in Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools, test every form end-to-end, confirm leads appear in Follow Up Boss, and confirm GA4 and Meta events fire.

### Prompt 14: Final QA

Act as a senior SEO and conversion-rate reviewer. Audit the entire codebase and live site behavior against these project rules. Check: every page has a CTA, every form posts correctly and has fallbacks, schema validates (list what to test in Google Rich Results Test), no duplicate titles or descriptions, no broken internal links, all `TODO` placeholders listed in one report, mobile layout on 375px width, and brokerage disclosures on every page. Output a prioritized fix list, then fix everything that can be fixed in code.
